@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title DELETE /api/workspace/v1/messenger/messages/[message_uuid]
actor "The client ." as Client
participant "WorkspaceMessageController\nRestAlchemy" as API
database "PostgreSQL\ncanonical lines + brackets" as DB
queue "Transactional outbox\n+ Typed tasks" as Outbox
participant "Background performers\nexact scope leases + fencing" as Worker
database "Ready projections\nThe container is tied up ." as Projection
database "The public events repository" as Events
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as Dispatcher
actor "The client . WebSocket" as WS
Client -> API: DELETE /api/workspace/v1/messenger/messages/{message_uuid}
API -> DB: resolve public placement; check active membership + generation
API -> DB: delete canonical MESSAGE root + immutable outbox events
DB --> API: The transaction is recorded
API --> Client: A successful public response
DB ->> Outbox: the event that was recorded
Outbox ->> Worker: read_counters / reaction_snapshot /\ndelivery_snapshot_event\neach task It has its own outbox_event_uuid
Worker -> Worker: topic: placements; user-stream/user-folder: aggregates
Worker -> Projection: Container counters after cleaning by external keys
Worker -> Events: message.deleted + container events\natomically in one. DB transaction with a projection
Events ->> Dispatcher: fixed ready line
Dispatcher ->> WS: I 'm going to send / repeat / reproduce
note over API,Worker
  Public ID = MESSAGE_PLACEMENT.uuid; canonical root It 's being deleted .
  Only after permission check through active membership.
  Lease/fencing, retry/backoff, DLQ/reaper - They 're compulsory ..
end note
@enduml
